              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جرثومة — jurthūma — \"a germ\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "يقتل الصابون الجراثيم. yaqtulu aṣ-ṣābūn al-jarāthīm. Soap kills germs."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: جراثيم, jarāthīm."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is mostly met in the plural جراثيم."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جرثومة (jurthūma) is built on a native four-letter root, j-r-th-m, where it named the root or origin of a thing; modern Arabic gave it the sense of a germ. The origin of the root itself is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
