          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تطعيم (taṭʿīm) is built on the native Arabic root ṭ-ʿ-m, \"to eat, to taste\" (Lane), the root of ṭaʿām, food. Lane gives Form II ṭaʿʿama as \"to graft\" a branch; modern Arabic uses the same word for putting a vaccine into the body."
            }
          ]
